<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Osismii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the far western tip of Brittany, the end of the known world for Greek and Roman geographers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Osismii lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finistere">Finistère</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotes-darmor">Côtes-d'Armor</a>. The Greek explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pytheas">Pytheas</a> probably referred to them as the Ostimioi around 320 BCE, placing them on a promontory facing the Ocean. Caesar lists them among the Armorican peoples.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their economy rested on farming, fishing and sea trade along the Atlantic route to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>. No ruler or central town is recorded before the conquest.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 57 BCE and supported the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a> in 56 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carhaix-plouguer">Vorgium</a> (Carhaix). In late antiquity their land was settled by migrants from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/domnonee">Domnonée</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cornouaille">Cornouaille</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/osismii.jpg" alt="Osismii" width="320" height="159"><figcaption>Image: cgb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stat%C3%A8re_d%27%C3%A9lectrum_%C3%A0_la_tente_et_%C3%A0_la_t%C3%AAte_coup%C3%A9e_frapp%C3%A9_par_les_Osismes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=osismii" aria-label="Osismii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4714 528 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Osismii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5034 784h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5034 784h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=osismii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

